WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:03.300
-Welcome to the show.
It is nice to meet you.

00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:04.634
Thank you so much for coming on.

00:00:04.634 --> 00:00:06.868
-Thank you for having me.
I've always wanted to do this.

00:00:06.868 --> 00:00:09.067
-Yeah.

00:00:09.067 --> 00:00:10.567
Yeah. Wow.
You did it right there.

00:00:10.567 --> 00:00:12.100
Yeah, you -- That's it.

00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:13.901
Thank you for
coming to New York.

00:00:13.901 --> 00:00:16.667
I know you're probably coming
from L.A. or Australia.

00:00:16.667 --> 00:00:18.100
-L.A.
-L.A., yeah.

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:20.000
Have you spent much time
in New York?

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:21.334
-I've spent a little bit
of time here.

00:00:21.334 --> 00:00:24.000
I try to come sort of
as often as possible

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:26.434
to see the plays
that are on and everything.

00:00:26.434 --> 00:00:30.267
But my parents are here,
and one of the biggest memories

00:00:30.267 --> 00:00:32.634
I have coming here
was when I was younger.

00:00:32.634 --> 00:00:33.868
And I came with them.
So this is one of my first --

00:00:33.868 --> 00:00:35.000
-Where is your mom?

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:36.367
-I'm trying to find them
while I'm speaking.

00:00:36.367 --> 00:00:37.834
-Oh, hey, there they are.
I see them.

00:00:37.834 --> 00:00:39.367
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yeah.

00:00:39.367 --> 00:00:42.200
-Hi, mom. Hi, dad.

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:44.300
Welcome to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:45.901
Yeah, it's also
their first time.

00:00:45.901 --> 00:00:47.200
-Yes.

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:48.901
-It's their first time
being on "The Tonight Show,"

00:00:48.901 --> 00:00:50.367
as well, which is perfect.

00:00:50.367 --> 00:00:51.667
-We're in it together.

00:00:51.667 --> 00:00:54.267
-When did you come to
the city with your parents?

00:00:54.267 --> 00:00:56.133
-I think I was 8 years old.

00:00:56.133 --> 00:00:58.734
And we sort of did all the
stuff, like all the sights.

00:00:58.734 --> 00:01:02.834
And I remember my dad sort of
surprised me with tickets

00:01:02.834 --> 00:01:05.067
to a Knicks game, because I was
a big basketball fan.

00:01:05.067 --> 00:01:06.234
-Oh, yeah, and where did --

00:01:06.234 --> 00:01:08.100
-Yeah, we were in
the nosebleeds, up the back,

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:10.467
but I remember it was just,
like -- It was, like --

00:01:10.467 --> 00:01:12.133
It was the most special
experience, though.

00:01:12.133 --> 00:01:13.534
You know what I mean?

00:01:13.534 --> 00:01:15.334
-Don't you have some news
to tell your parents?

00:01:15.334 --> 00:01:18.801
-Yeah. We're going to the Knicks
tomorrow, but way closer.

00:01:18.801 --> 00:01:21.567
[ Applause ]

00:01:21.567 --> 00:01:25.100
-Yeah, that's right. Way closer.

00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:26.801
-Yeah.

00:01:28.267 --> 00:01:30.834
-Now, the new season
of "Euphoria"

00:01:30.834 --> 00:01:33.567
had a giant premiere on Sunday.

00:01:33.567 --> 00:01:34.767
Congratulations.
-Thank you.

00:01:34.767 --> 00:01:36.934
-It's become a huge, huge hit.

00:01:36.934 --> 00:01:39.434
Did you have any idea
that it would be this big

00:01:39.434 --> 00:01:41.267
the second time around,
the second season?

00:01:41.267 --> 00:01:44.133
-No, I didn't know, and then
they told me this morning

00:01:44.133 --> 00:01:47.100
that it, like,
crashed the website.

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:50.300
And, you know, a lot of people
have seen it, so it's -- Yeah.

00:01:50.300 --> 00:01:52.934
It's so scary.
-I'll tell you what's scary.

00:01:52.934 --> 00:01:55.167
You're getting your own
wax figure at Madame Tussauds.

00:01:55.167 --> 00:01:56.667
-Yeah.

00:01:56.667 --> 00:02:02.033
-Now, I'm lucky enough to be --
I've done it myself, as well.

00:02:02.033 --> 00:02:03.234
Have you been through the
whole process yet?

00:02:03.234 --> 00:02:04.501
-I did.

00:02:04.501 --> 00:02:06.067
I went through the process,
and it was strange,

00:02:06.067 --> 00:02:09.334
but the strangest thing is their
shirts that the crew wear

00:02:09.334 --> 00:02:13.868
say like, "Paparazzi" and
like, "Celebrity."

00:02:13.868 --> 00:02:15.567
That was the
strangest thing for me.

00:02:15.567 --> 00:02:17.400
Like, you've got all these
cameras in front of you

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:18.934
and you've got all these
little dots on your face.

00:02:18.934 --> 00:02:22.200
It looks like behind the scenes
of "Planet of the Apes."

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:23.834
And then these people
in shirts that say like

00:02:23.834 --> 00:02:25.200
"Paparazzi"
and like, "Celebrity."

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:27.300
-Really? I didn't see that...
-Yeah, it was peculiar.

00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:30.834
-...on mine.
-Great people.

00:02:30.834 --> 00:02:34.033
-I don't know if you have
legit people doing it.

00:02:34.033 --> 00:02:36.868
-It's like a gang of paparazzi
just, like,

00:02:36.868 --> 00:02:38.767
gluing a picture.

00:02:38.767 --> 00:02:41.234
-It turns out your
wax figure is this big.

00:02:41.234 --> 00:02:44.467
-Yeah, it's a bobblehead.
-It's LEGOs. Yeah, exactly.

00:02:44.467 --> 00:02:46.300
This show, "Euphoria,"
I will say,

00:02:46.300 --> 00:02:48.534
is pretty dark at some parts,

00:02:48.534 --> 00:02:50.567
pretty, you know --

00:02:50.567 --> 00:02:53.133
It must be stressful
to do a show like this.

00:02:53.133 --> 00:02:55.334
But I heard that
to keep it loose,

00:02:55.334 --> 00:02:57.000
you would do you this thing
where you would grab

00:02:57.000 --> 00:02:59.200
people's phones and just take
selfies with their phones?

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:01.300
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:03:01.300 --> 00:03:03.234
-Now, how do you go with that --
I like the bit,

00:03:03.234 --> 00:03:04.501
but what is it?

00:03:04.501 --> 00:03:05.901
-Well, it's not even, like,
"Euphoria"-specific.

00:03:05.901 --> 00:03:09.133
I think was in New York a couple
of weeks ago and I was at a bar,

00:03:09.133 --> 00:03:12.667
and someone had left their phone
sort of on a table somewhere.

00:03:12.667 --> 00:03:14.100
And I kind of just, like --
There's something about it.

00:03:14.100 --> 00:03:15.434
Like, I want them to find it.

00:03:15.434 --> 00:03:16.734
I have this idea
that they're going to have

00:03:16.734 --> 00:03:18.767
the phone for like 40 years,
and in 40 years' time,

00:03:18.767 --> 00:03:19.901
they're going to be like,

00:03:19.901 --> 00:03:21.467
"Oh, I'm going to go through
my camera roll,"

00:03:21.467 --> 00:03:23.067
like they don't
go through it every day,

00:03:23.067 --> 00:03:24.734
and be like, "Oh, my God.

00:03:24.734 --> 00:03:27.467
Who is this?"

00:03:27.467 --> 00:03:28.534
-No, they know who you are.

00:03:28.534 --> 00:03:30.334
But you just grab
a phone and just --

00:03:30.334 --> 00:03:31.934
-Yeah, like,
but I don't move it,

00:03:31.934 --> 00:03:33.868
because I don't
want to be invasive.

00:03:33.868 --> 00:03:37.467
So I do the slide up.

00:03:37.467 --> 00:03:39.734
-Oh, that's very nice of you.
I appreciate that.

00:03:39.734 --> 00:03:42.200
Yeah, thoughtful.
-Yeah, like a pigeon.

00:03:42.200 --> 00:03:45.400
-Yeah, very thoughtful of you
to do that, yeah.

00:03:45.400 --> 00:03:48.601
In this show,
you play Nate, who --

00:03:48.601 --> 00:03:50.968
He's not really a good guy.

00:03:50.968 --> 00:03:52.567
No.

00:03:52.567 --> 00:03:55.334
But at the end of
Sunday's episode,

00:03:55.334 --> 00:03:57.901
your character is
a little changed kind of.

00:03:57.901 --> 00:03:58.934
Well --
-Yeah.

00:03:58.934 --> 00:04:01.834
-He gets beat up.
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:04:01.834 --> 00:04:04.801
-But fans were like,
"Well, he had it coming."

00:04:04.801 --> 00:04:07.167
-Yeah, they were stoked.
They were so happy about it.

00:04:07.167 --> 00:04:08.901
-And would you agree with that?

00:04:08.901 --> 00:04:11.534
-Well...

00:04:11.534 --> 00:04:12.834
-I mean, it is you.

00:04:12.834 --> 00:04:16.367
-I think me as Jacob,
I would love to beat him up.

00:04:16.367 --> 00:04:18.367
Like, I would love to give him
a clip around the ears.

00:04:18.367 --> 00:04:22.167
But as Nate, you know,
I feel very bad for him.

00:04:22.167 --> 00:04:24.234
-Yeah, because you are
his character.

00:04:24.234 --> 00:04:25.234
You're playing
the character so well.

00:04:25.234 --> 00:04:26.667
-Yeah, I had to get beat up.

00:04:26.667 --> 00:04:27.667
-Yeah, and you don't want to get
beat up, but --

00:04:27.667 --> 00:04:30.367
-It sucked.
-Yeah.

00:04:30.367 --> 00:04:32.667
I want to show everyone
a clip from the show.

00:04:32.667 --> 00:04:35.334
Here's Jacob Elordi in
the new season of "Euphoria."

00:04:35.334 --> 00:04:36.367
Take a look at this.

00:04:37.734 --> 00:04:38.767
-What's up, man?

00:04:38.767 --> 00:04:40.334
You having a good time?

00:04:40.334 --> 00:04:43.534
-[ Coughs ] Yeah.

00:04:43.534 --> 00:04:46.033
-You make any
New Year's resolutions?

00:04:46.033 --> 00:04:47.100
-No.

00:04:47.100 --> 00:04:48.467
You?

00:04:48.467 --> 00:04:50.934
-A few.

00:04:50.934 --> 00:04:54.701
-The last time we talked, didn't
you say you wanted to kill me?

00:04:54.701 --> 00:04:55.767
-[ Chuckles ]

00:04:55.767 --> 00:05:00.267
Yeah, well,
to a new year, playboy.

00:05:03.501 --> 00:05:04.868
-Oh, my God!

00:05:04.868 --> 00:05:06.501
-Jacob Elordi, everybody.

00:05:06.501 --> 00:05:09.801
"Euphoria" airs Sundays
at 9:00 p.m. on HBO.

